export default [{"s":1.1,"e":2.65,"t":"Episode one."},{"s":2.7,"e":4.74,"t":"Where to start reading X-Men..."},{"s":4.82,"e":6.58,"t":"without losing your mind."},{"s":6.996,"e":11.586,"t":"A few years ago, after a long stretch away from comics, I walked into Graham"},{"s":11.636,"e":15.986,"t":"Crackers Comics in Chicago and asked the guy behind the counter the question every"},{"s":16.036,"e":18.876,"t":"lapsed fan is a little embarrassed to ask."},{"s":19.076,"e":21.346,"t":"Where do I get back into X-Men?"},{"s":21.396,"e":24.546,"t":"Because X-Men is 60 years of comics."},{"s":24.596,"e":27.026,"t":"A dozen books with X-Men in the title."},{"s":27.076,"e":30.396,"t":"And reading orders online that look like tax forms."},{"s":30.516,"e":32.306,"t":"He didn't hand me a reading order."},{"s":32.356,"e":34.146,"t":"He handed me one book."},{"s":34.196,"e":35.436,"t":"And it worked."},{"s":35.776,"e":37.646,"t":"So that's what this video is."},{"s":37.696,"e":39.086,"t":"Not a reading order."},{"s":39.136,"e":41.326,"t":"Five books. One shelf."},{"s":41.376,"e":42.696,"t":"Let's get into it."},{"s":43.135,"e":44.245,"t":"Quick background."},{"s":44.295,"e":49.885,"t":"I was eight years old, growing up in Chicagoland, in 1992, when X-Men: The Animated"},{"s":49.935,"e":51.285,"t":"Series came on..."},{"s":51.335,"e":53.645,"t":"and flipped a switch in my brain."},{"s":53.695,"e":58.695,"t":"That theme song still lives rent free, and it gets me pumped every single time."},{"s":59.114,"e":61.704,"t":"My best friend is the one who got us all into it."},{"s":61.754,"e":64.584,"t":"The cartoon, the comics, all of it."},{"s":64.634,"e":66.354,"t":"So he got first pick..."},{"s":66.434,"e":68.184,"t":"and he picked Gambit."},{"s":68.234,"e":72.584,"t":"Obviously. Gambit and Wolverine were the coolest guys on the show."},{"s":72.634,"e":76.984,"t":"And Gambit had the trench coat, the glowing cards, and an accent none of us could"},{"s":77.034,"e":78.194,"t":"understand."},{"s":78.354,"e":81.984,"t":"He also decided the girl everybody in class had a crush on..."},{"s":82.034,"e":83.314,"t":"was Rogue."},{"s":84.314,"e":85.394,"t":"Kids."},{"s":85.83,"e":87.62,"t":"I got Colossus."},{"s":87.67,"e":89.38,"t":"And I felt cheated."},{"s":89.43,"e":94.5,"t":"Big Russian guy, turns into steel, says about four words an episode..."},{"s":94.55,"e":96.02,"t":"but he was mine."},{"s":96.07,"e":97.38,"t":"So I stuck with him."},{"s":97.43,"e":101.14,"t":"And somewhere along the way, I actually started to care about him."},{"s":101.19,"e":102.94,"t":"Strongest guy in the room..."},{"s":102.99,"e":105.07,"t":"and he'd rather be home painting."},{"s":105.492,"e":108.162,"t":"I don't think I'm the only one this happened to."},{"s":108.212,"e":110.402,"t":"A lot of us didn't pick our X-Man."},{"s":110.452,"e":113.762,"t":"We got handed one, and then we got attached."},{"s":113.812,"e":115.602,"t":"That's how I got into X-Men."},{"s":115.652,"e":117.202,"t":"Not through a reading order."},{"s":117.252,"e":118.732,"t":"Through a character."},{"s":118.932,"e":119.922,"t":"Hold on to that."},{"s":119.972,"e":121.932,"t":"I'm gonna come back to it in a minute."},{"s":122.281,"e":125.031,"t":"The obvious move is to start at the beginning."},{"s":125.081,"e":126.712,"t":"X-Men number one."},{"s":126.762,"e":130.071,"t":"1963. It matters historically."},{"s":130.121,"e":131.992,"t":"Stan Lee and Jack Kirby."},{"s":132.042,"e":133.512,"t":"The original five."},{"s":133.562,"e":135.591,"t":"Magneto's first appearance."},{"s":135.641,"e":138.552,"t":"Honestly? It feels like a different team."},{"s":138.602,"e":141.911,"t":"But it's good background, and it matters more than you'd think once we get to"},{"s":141.961,"e":144.322,"t":"Hickman. Hold that thought, too."},{"s":144.739,"e":148.409,"t":"But historically important and a good first read..."},{"s":148.459,"e":150.209,"t":"are not the same thing."},{"s":150.259,"e":153.369,"t":"The storytelling has changed a lot in 60 years."},{"s":153.419,"e":156.459,"t":"And you don't need to do homework to enjoy this stuff."},{"s":156.539,"e":158.729,"t":"So treat it like a tasting menu."},{"s":158.779,"e":161.009,"t":"Five stories, from different eras."},{"s":161.059,"e":163.009,"t":"If one grabs you, follow it."},{"s":163.059,"e":165.009,"t":"If one doesn't, skip it."},{"s":165.059,"e":166.539,"t":"Nobody's checking."},{"s":166.884,"e":169.954,"t":"Number one. The Dark Phoenix Saga."},{"s":170.004,"e":173.554,"t":"Uncanny X-Men 129 through 137."},{"s":173.604,"e":177.074,"t":"1980. Chris Claremont and John Byrne."},{"s":177.124,"e":179.954,"t":"If you only read one X-Men story..."},{"s":180.004,"e":181.714,"t":"it's probably this one."},{"s":181.764,"e":183.714,"t":"It's the team at their peak."},{"s":183.764,"e":187.244,"t":"And it's where a lot of what you know about the X-Men comes from."},{"s":187.591,"e":192.101,"t":"Issue 129 alone introduces Kitty Pryde and Emma Frost."},{"s":192.151,"e":194.261,"t":"130 gives you Dazzler..."},{"s":194.311,"e":196.341,"t":"who's a disco superhero."},{"s":196.391,"e":198.501,"t":"And it's not as corny as it sounds."},{"s":198.551,"e":201.061,"t":"But the real story is Jean Grey."},{"s":201.111,"e":203.141,"t":"She's gained cosmic power."},{"s":203.191,"e":205.461,"t":"The Hellfire Club messes with her head."},{"s":205.511,"e":207.951,"t":"And it goes about as well as you'd expect."},{"s":208.299,"e":213.089,"t":"What makes it hold up is that it's not just a big fight, like Secret Wars."},{"s":213.139,"e":216.499,"t":"It's a team, trying to save a friend from herself."},{"s":216.579,"e":217.779,"t":"And then..."},{"s":218.139,"e":221.342,"t":"137. I'm not gonna spoil it for you."},{"s":221.392,"e":225.939,"t":"I'll just say it's one of the most famous endings in comics, for a reason."},{"s":226.368,"e":230.478,"t":"I'd been through the Phoenix story a bunch of times before I ever read the actual"},{"s":230.528,"e":235.278,"t":"book. The cartoon did it, and honestly, did it really well."},{"s":235.328,"e":237.398,"t":"The movies have tried it twice..."},{"s":237.448,"e":240.078,"t":"and I'm still waiting for one to get it right."},{"s":240.128,"e":241.358,"t":"But it didn't matter."},{"s":241.408,"e":245.918,"t":"Even knowing how it ends, the trade paperback is still the best way to experience"},{"s":245.968,"e":247.918,"t":"it. Team dynamics."},{"s":247.968,"e":249.598,"t":"Real consequences."},{"s":249.648,"e":253.838,"t":"And a character arc that people are still adapting 40 years later."},{"s":253.888,"e":255.598,"t":"If you start anywhere..."},{"s":255.648,"e":256.728,"t":"start here."},{"s":257.159,"e":259.989,"t":"Number two. Days of Future Past."},{"s":260.039,"e":263.359,"t":"Uncanny X-Men 141 and 142."},{"s":263.559,"e":264.549,"t":"Short and sweet."},{"s":264.599,"e":266.949,"t":"Two issues. That covers the whole pitch."},{"s":266.999,"e":272.069,"t":"A future where the Sentinels won, and most of the X-Men are dead, or in camps."},{"s":272.119,"e":275.669,"t":"Kitty's mind gets sent back to the present to stop it from happening."},{"s":275.719,"e":277.589,"t":"It's short. It's dark."},{"s":277.639,"e":281.589,"t":"And it's the blueprint for every stop-the-bad-future story the X-Men have done"},{"s":281.639,"e":283.949,"t":"since. Including the movie..."},{"s":283.999,"e":286.959,"t":"and the cartoon episode you probably saw first."},{"s":287.375,"e":288.525,"t":"Number three."},{"s":288.575,"e":290.365,"t":"X-Cutioner's Song."},{"s":290.415,"e":293.005,"t":"This one's for the kids who grew up on the cartoon."},{"s":293.055,"e":297.965,"t":"'92 into'93. A crossover across four X-books."},{"s":298.015,"e":303.005,"t":"Professor X gets shot, Cable's the main suspect, and it turns into a whole mess with"},{"s":303.055,"e":304.738,"t":"Stryfe and Apocalypse."},{"s":304.788,"e":307.965,"t":"It is the most'90s thing you will ever read."},{"s":308.015,"e":309.405,"t":"Everybody's squinting."},{"s":309.455,"e":311.058,"t":"Everybody has pouches."},{"s":311.108,"e":312.445,"t":"It's pretty rad."},{"s":312.495,"e":316.365,"t":"If the cartoon is your X-Men, this is the comic that feels like it."},{"s":316.415,"e":317.445,"t":"Fair warning..."},{"s":317.495,"e":322.405,"t":"it is messy. It jumps across four different books, so grab the trade paperback."},{"s":322.455,"e":324.455,"t":"Puts everything in order for you."},{"s":324.801,"e":328.351,"t":"Number four. God Loves, Man Kills."},{"s":328.401,"e":329.711,"t":"1982."},{"s":329.761,"e":332.111,"t":"Chris Claremont and Brent Anderson."},{"s":332.161,"e":334.031,"t":"A standalone graphic novel."},{"s":334.081,"e":335.551,"t":"No continuity homework."},{"s":335.601,"e":338.271,"t":"You pick it up, you read it, you're done."},{"s":338.321,"e":343.071,"t":"A preacher named William Stryker starts a crusade against mutants, and the X-Men end"},{"s":343.121,"e":345.391,"t":"up working with Magneto to stop him."},{"s":345.441,"e":349.471,"t":"This is the X-Men at their most direct about what they've always been about."},{"s":349.521,"e":351.311,"t":"Fear. Prejudice."},{"s":351.361,"e":353.631,"t":"People being hated for what they are."},{"s":353.681,"e":357.631,"t":"It's also the backbone of the second X-Men movie, if that's your entry point."},{"s":357.681,"e":362.361,"t":"It's heavy. But it's the one that shows you why these stories still matter."},{"s":362.801,"e":365.231,"t":"Number five. House of M."},{"s":365.281,"e":370.671,"t":"2005. The legendary Brian Michael Bendis, and Olivier Coipel."},{"s":370.721,"e":373.431,"t":"This is the book the guy at Graham Crackers handed me."},{"s":373.481,"e":376.031,"t":"The Scarlet Witch rewrites reality."},{"s":376.081,"e":379.401,"t":"Everybody wakes up in a world where they got what they wanted..."},{"s":379.561,"e":382.671,"t":"and a few of them start to realize something's wrong."},{"s":382.721,"e":387.751,"t":"It's an event book, so it's big, and loud, and it touches the Avengers too."},{"s":387.801,"e":392.151,"t":"But it reads clean, and it was the perfect way back in for me as a young adult."},{"s":392.201,"e":395.311,"t":"And the ending changed the X-Men for about a decade."},{"s":395.361,"e":398.361,"t":"Three words. You'll know them when you see them."},{"s":398.791,"e":402.981,"t":"Once you've got a few of these under your belt, then read House of X and Powers of"},{"s":403.031,"e":403.871,"t":"X."},{"s":404.151,"e":406.901,"t":"2019. Jonathan Hickman."},{"s":406.951,"e":411.221,"t":"It's 12 issues that flip decades of X-Men history on its head."},{"s":411.271,"e":413.141,"t":"Remember X-Men number one?"},{"s":413.191,"e":417.341,"t":"This is where Xavier's choices, going all the way back to the beginning, start"},{"s":417.391,"e":418.501,"t":"catching up with him."},{"s":418.551,"e":419.941,"t":"It's brilliant."},{"s":419.991,"e":421.391,"t":"And it's also..."},{"s":421.471,"e":422.671,"t":"a lot."},{"s":422.791,"e":426.581,"t":"It lands so much harder when you know who these people are, and what they've been"},{"s":426.631,"e":428.981,"t":"through. So don't start there."},{"s":429.031,"e":430.991,"t":"Save it. It'll be waiting."},{"s":431.41,"e":433.6,"t":"And here's my actual advice."},{"s":433.65,"e":435.12,"t":"Shop like a kid."},{"s":435.17,"e":437.76,"t":"When you were 10, you didn't need a reading order."},{"s":437.81,"e":441.04,"t":"You grabbed whatever cover looked cool, and figured it out."},{"s":441.09,"e":442.72,"t":"Find a character you like."},{"s":442.77,"e":444.6,"t":"For me, it was Colossus..."},{"s":444.65,"e":446.24,"t":"and I didn't even pick him."},{"s":446.29,"e":448.16,"t":"For you, it might be Storm."},{"s":448.21,"e":449.68,"t":"Then you can follow them."},{"s":449.73,"e":450.88,"t":"Read their stories."},{"s":450.93,"e":452.96,"t":"Jump around. Get confused."},{"s":453.01,"e":454.08,"t":"Look stuff up."},{"s":454.13,"e":455.69,"t":"That's half the fun."},{"s":456.114,"e":461.104,"t":"Quick note. I built ComixCatalog because I wanted one place to track what I own, and"},{"s":461.154,"e":462.304,"t":"what I'm hunting."},{"s":462.354,"e":466.504,"t":"You can search any of these books, see the covers, and throw the ones you want on a"},{"s":466.554,"e":470.544,"t":"wantlist, so you're not standing in a shop trying to remember issue numbers."},{"s":470.594,"e":471.824,"t":"It's free to use."},{"s":471.874,"e":472.954,"t":"Link's below."},{"s":473.374,"e":475.004,"t":"So, the shelf."},{"s":475.054,"e":476.284,"t":"Dark Phoenix."},{"s":476.334,"e":477.884,"t":"Days of Future Past."},{"s":477.934,"e":479.564,"t":"X-Cutioner's Song."},{"s":479.614,"e":481.644,"t":"God Loves, Man Kills."},{"s":481.694,"e":483.204,"t":"And House of M."},{"s":483.254,"e":486.764,"t":"And then House of X and Powers of X, when you're ready."},{"s":486.814,"e":489.244,"t":"Don't turn reading comics into homework."},{"s":489.294,"e":490.604,"t":"Go pick up a comic..."},{"s":490.654,"e":493.494,"t":"and come back and tell me which one you started with."}];
